==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named after [[w:Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt|Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt]] and [[w:Alfons Maria Jakob|Alfons Maria Jakob]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=Creutzfeldt-Jakob [[disease]]|-}} (''abbreviation'' '''[[CJD]]''')

# {{context|disease|neurology|lang=en}} A [[rare]], [[progressive]], [[fatal]] [[disease]] of the [[nervous system]], characterized by [[dementia]] and loss of [[muscle]] [[control]]. It is a [[prion]] disease, apparently transmissible from animals to humans by eating infected tissue, as well as from tissue interchanges among humans (e.g. corneal transplants, blood transfusions).

